%I A398414 #28 Sep 08 2026 22:58:18
%S A398414 2,3,5,19,37,73,29,23,7,13,17,11,43,229,457,83,331,661,1321,139,277,
%T A398414 79,157,313,2503,47,31,61,487,59,41,163,1303,521,347,3701,2467,4933,
%U A398414 1973,263,1051,191,127,677,2707,5413,433,173,691,1381
%N A398414 a(1) = 2. For n > 1, choose the least k >= 1 such that 2^k*a(n-1) - 1 has a prime factor not previously occurring in the sequence; a(n) is the least such unused factor.
%C A398414 Question: Will all primes appear in this sequence?
%e A398414 From a(1) = 2, k = 1: 2^1*2 - 1 = 3. The prime factor 3 is unused. Therefore, a(2) = 3.
%e A398414 From a(2) = 3, k = 1: 2*3 - 1 = 5. Since 5 is unused, a(3) = 5.
%e A398414 From a(3) = 5, k = 1: 2*5 - 1 = 9 = 3^2. The prime 3 is already used, so this fails.
%e A398414 k = 2: 4 * 5 - 1 = 19. The prime 19 is unused. Therefore, a(4) = 19.
%o A398414 (PARI) isok(k, prev, vs) = my(vp=factor(2^k*prev - 1)[,1]); for (i=1, #vp, if (!vecsearch(vs, vp[i]), return(vp[i])); );
%o A398414 lista(nn) = my(v=vector(nn), vs); v[1] = 2; for(n=2, nn, vs = vecsort(v); my(k=1, d); while (!(d=isok(k, v[n-1], vs)), k++); v[n] = d; ); v; \\ _Michel Marcus_, Aug 31 2026
%Y A398414 Cf. A174161, A399458.
%K A398414 nonn,new
